Let lookup() report "no valid contact" when none of the bindings is valid.

lookup() picks the first binding of the IMPU that is VALID_CONTACT - not
expired, not pending delete or notify - by walking linked_contacts and
breaking out of the loop on a match:

	while(impucontact && (ptr = impucontact->contact)) {
		if(VALID_UE_TYPE(...) && VALID_CONTACT(...) && allowed_method(...))
			break;
		impucontact = impucontact->next;
	}
	if(ptr == 0)
		goto done;          /* "No contacts founds" */

ptr is assigned on every iteration, before the test, so a walk that runs off
the end without a match leaves it on the LAST binding it examined, not on
NULL. The ptr == 0 check then only catches a record with no bindings at all;
a record whose bindings are all dead falls through, and lookup() rewrites
the Request-URI to the last dead one and returns 1.

A record like that is not rare. The IMPU stays IMPU_REGISTERED from the
moment its last binding expires or is de-registered until the usrloc timer
next processes it, so every terminating request in that window is routed to
an address the UE has left instead of being answered as unregistered, and
route[REBIND] in serving.cfg - which uses lookup() to find the bindings a new
registration supersedes - was handed that dead binding, re-injected it with
expires=1 and so revived it for a second, with a round of NOTIFYs each time.
Measured on KinD: a REGISTER a few seconds after the previous registration's
de-REGISTER retired <sip:10.10.0.18:5088>, which was already in
CONTACT_NOTIFY_READY, with no "Found a valid contact" logged for it.

term_impu_has_contact() walks the same list the right way - its ret is set
only inside the matching branch - so only lookup() needs the fix: a walk
that reached the end of the list found nothing.

diff --git a/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/lookup.c b/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/lookup.c
--- a/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/lookup.c
+++ b/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/lookup.c
@@ -149,6 +149,12 @@
 		impucontact = impucontact->next;
 	}
 
+	/* The walk leaves ptr on the last contact it examined, valid or not: only
+	 * a walk that stopped before the end of the list found one. Without this a
+	 * record holding nothing but dead bindings routes to the last of them. */
+	if(!impucontact)
+		ptr = 0;
+
 	/* look first for an un-expired and supported contact */
 	if(ptr == 0) {
 		LM_INFO("No contacts founds for IMPU <%.*s>\n", aor.len, aor.s);
